From e7931702dd3d40e0b0871cec5d358ef467ba5a81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DaffyDabz <daffydabz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 13:52:44 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 348/371] pirates: Port Royal has fishing spots on the piers; a
 pirate walks up, gets a rod, casts, reels in a fish and is paid gold, as
 server-tree patch 0432

Fishing lane: ported and trimmed from the 2013 Pirates Online fishing minigame (one pirate per spot, no
bait/lure/rod inventory, no legendary fish, no tutorials). DistributedFishingSpot is a new LAST class in
pirates.dc, so no existing class or field number moves; GameAreaBuilderAI builds the pier spots from
PortRoyalIsland's FishingSpot objects (want-fishing, default on). Client half = client patch 45 (v488).
Lane tests: AI test FAIL on 1013db7 -> 0 failures; client test 20 failures -> 0. Needs astrond + UberDOG
+ AI restart. Undo: want-fishing 0 + AI restart.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
